From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 22:04:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/11] RISC OS: shut down before exit(), not from atexit()

systemShutdown() ran from atexit() and joins the path-finding thread.
UnixLib (before riscos-unixlib 7d875c1) can't switch threads while exit()
runs, so quitting the game ended in "Aborted". It now runs just before
main() returns, which works with any UnixLib.
---
 src/main.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
index 9f79839..986b89a 100644
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -1311,7 +1311,14 @@ int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 	debug_MEMSTATS();
 #endif
 
+#if defined(WZ_OS_RISCOS)
+	// Shut down now rather than from atexit(): UnixLib can't switch
+	// threads while exit() runs, so joining the path-finding thread there
+	// stopped the program with "Aborted".
+	systemShutdown();
+#else
 	atexit(systemShutdown);
+#endif
 	return EXIT_SUCCESS;
 }
 
